# DreamRate project rules

## Before every commit (and push)

Run these from `dream-rate-ui/` and make sure they pass before running `git commit`:

1. `npm run check` - must exit 0 (currently 0 errors, 0 warnings).
2. `npm run build` - the production build must succeed. It runs `wrangler types` first, which regenerates `worker-configuration.d.ts`.

Do not commit or push if any of these fail. Fix the problem first, or tell the user why it can't be fixed.

Do NOT run `wrangler types --check` as a gate (it was removed from `npm run check` and `npm run build`). Its result depends on which gitignored env files (`.env`, `.env.local`, `.dev.vars`) exist on the machine, so it passes locally and fails on the build server.

`worker-configuration.d.ts` is regenerated by every build, so local runs will modify it. Do not commit those changes unless `wrangler.jsonc` changed; restore it with `git checkout -- dream-rate-ui/worker-configuration.d.ts` instead.

## Commit style

Use conventional commits, matching the existing history (for example `feat(mobile): ...`, `fix(auth): ...`, `chore: ...`).
